(Connected with the Prākṛta {#laqaha#} which appears
 to be derived from it) Charming, handsome, beautiful, attractive, lovely;
 {#atikrAntaH kAlo lawaBalalanABogasulaBaH#} <ls>Bh. 3. 32</ls> (where commentators
 render {#lawaBa#} by {#salAvaRya#}); {#tasyAH pAdanaKaSreRiH SoBate lawaBaBruvaH#}
 <ls>Vikr. 8. 6</ls>. Bilhaṇa has used this word in three more places of the same
 book, where it appears to mean ‘a young pretty woman’, ‘a handsome woman’;
 {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%} {#kiM vA varRanayA samastalawaBAlaMkAratAmezyati#} <ls n="Vikr.">8. 86</ls>; {#anarDyalAvaRyaniDAnaBUmirna#}
 {#kasya loBaM lawaBA tanoti#} <ls n="Vikr.">9. 68</ls>; {#keSabanDaviBavErlawaBAnAM piRqatAmiva#}
 {#jagAma tamisram#} <ls n="Vikr.">11. 18</ls>.
